WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.060
One photo, one sentence,

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.060
and an AI designed this toy.

00:00:04.074 --> 00:00:06.834
An AI looked at one photo and designed this toy.

00:00:06.861 --> 00:00:09.721
This toy was designed by an AI that saw one photo.

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:12.663
But OpenAI put one tiny line under this demo.

00:00:13.123 --> 00:00:13.803
Keep your eye on it.

00:00:13.827 --> 00:00:16.107
This is GPT 6.1 Tera.

00:00:16.327 --> 00:00:17.347
It's not built to chat,

00:00:17.427 --> 00:00:19.007
it's built to use your computer.

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:21.178
This is GPT 6.1 Tera.

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:22.498
It's not built to chat.

00:00:22.678 --> 00:00:24.118
It's built to use your computer.

00:00:24.146 --> 00:00:26.126
Here, it opens a 3D app and

00:00:26.206 --> 00:00:28.306
builds the tram piece by piece.

00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:30.033
It's half the price of the last Terra,

00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:32.873
and OpenAI says it finishes tasks three

00:00:32.953 --> 00:00:35.073
times faster than its bigger models.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.220
Now, that tiny line, shown at actual speed,

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.540
some sections omitted,

00:00:39.568 --> 00:00:42.248
Actual speed, with the slow parts cut out.

00:00:42.266 --> 00:00:43.746
And three times faster?

00:00:44.106 --> 00:00:45.846
That's OpenAI's own test.

00:00:46.106 --> 00:00:48.266
No one outside OpenAI has confirmed it yet.

00:00:48.278 --> 00:00:49.658
A demo is an ad.

00:00:49.738 --> 00:00:50.858
Read the line under it.

00:00:50.886 --> 00:00:51.966
Seen a demo like this?

00:00:52.046 --> 00:00:53.006
Send it our way.

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:53.806
We'll check it.
